{
  "lesson_id": "b2_verb_object_infinitive_gerund",
  "level": "B2",
  "title": "Verb + object + infinitive/gerund: Verb patterns",
  "description": "Некоторые verbs принимают object, после которого идёт infinitive или -ing. Форма зависит от конкретного verb pattern.",
  "theory": {
    "rule_id": "RULE-B2-13-RU",
    "lesson_num": 13,
    "title": "Правила: Verb + object + infinitive/gerund: Verb patterns",
    "level": "B2",
    "overview": "Некоторые verbs принимают object, после которого идёт infinitive или -ing. Форма зависит от конкретного verb pattern.",
    "main_rule": "want/expect/allow/encourage + object + to V1. catch/find/keep + object + V-ing. make/let + object + bare infinitive. Remember can change meaning depending on pattern.",
    "form": "verb + object + to V1. verb + object + V-ing. make/let + object + V1.",
    "when_why": "Учите весь pattern: verb + object + next verb form.",
    "examples": "The manager encouraged us to apply. → Менеджер encouraged нас подать заявку.\nI found him working late. → Я обнаружил, что он работает допоздна.\nThe manager made us wait. → Менеджер заставил нас ждать.\nThey let us leave early. → Они позволили нам уйти раньше.\nI remember meeting her. → Я помню, как встретил её.\nI remembered to call her. → Я не забыл ей позвонить.",
    "special_cases": "Remember + -ing = memory of past event. Remember + to V1 = remember a future/necessary action. Bare infinitive appears after make/let in this pattern.",
    "common_mistakes": "❌ She encouraged me apply. → ✅ She encouraged me to apply.\n❌ They made us to wait. → ✅ They made us wait.\n❌ I remember to meeting her. → ✅ I remember meeting her.",
    "dont_confuse": "Сначала определяй first verb, object и pattern после object.",
    "quick_summary": "want/expect/allow/encourage + object + to.\ncatch/find/keep + object + -ing.\nmake/let + object + V1."
  },
